<div class="stonetop-migration">

	<p class="stonetop-migration-lead">
		Stonetop is changing the ID it uses to store your campaign. Your world, its name, its
		folder and everything in it stay exactly where they are. Only the label Foundry uses
		to connect this world to the system changes, from
		<code>{{this.oldId}}</code> to <code>{{this.newId}}</code>.
	</p>

	{{#if isBlocked}}
		<section class="stonetop-migration-panel is-blocked">
			<h3>Not ready yet</h3>
			<p>Sort these out and then check again:</p>
			<ul>
				{{#each blockers}}<li>{{this}}</li>{{/each}}
			</ul>
		</section>
	{{/if}}

	{{#if isReady}}
		{{#if warnings.length}}
			<section class="stonetop-migration-panel is-warning">
				<ul>
					{{#each warnings}}<li>{{this}}</li>{{/each}}
				</ul>
			</section>
		{{/if}}

		<section class="stonetop-migration-panel">
			{{#if isHosted}}
				<h3>Hosted Foundry: two steps, not one</h3>
				<p>
					Pointing a world at a different system needs Foundry's own setup screen, and
					hosted services replace that with their own. So this window does the data half
					here and now, and you finish by hand afterwards. The steps appear here when
					this part is done.
				</p>
			{{else}}
				<h3>What will happen</h3>
				<ol>
					<li>Your campaign data is <strong>copied</strong> into the new name. Nothing is deleted.</li>
					<li>This world is pointed at the renamed system.</li>
					<li>Foundry returns you to the setup screen. Launch the world again and it finishes.</li>
				</ol>
			{{/if}}
			<p class="stonetop-migration-counts">
				{{preview.documents}} documents and {{preview.settings}} settings to copy,
				across {{preview.locations}} places in this world.
				{{#if preview.alreadyDone}}({{preview.alreadyDone}} already done.){{/if}}
			</p>
			{{#if isHosted}}
				<p class="stonetop-migration-note">
					Nothing is deleted and nothing is moved. This world still runs on
					<code>{{this.oldId}}</code> when it finishes, so stopping here leaves you exactly
					where you started. Take a backup or Save Point first all the same.
				</p>
			{{else}}
				<p class="stonetop-migration-note">
					Take a backup first if you have not already: return to setup, right-click this
					world and choose <strong>Take Backup</strong>. That is the only real undo.
				</p>
			{{/if}}
		</section>
	{{/if}}

	{{#if isConfirming}}
		<section class="stonetop-migration-panel is-confirm">
			<h3>Ready when you are</h3>
			<p>
				This cannot be undone from inside Foundry. Once it starts, this world is pointed
				at <code>{{this.newId}}</code> and Foundry returns you to the setup screen.
			</p>
			<p class="stonetop-migration-note">
				If you have not taken a backup yet, choose Cancel and take one first.
			</p>
		</section>
	{{/if}}

	{{#if isRunning}}
		<section class="stonetop-migration-panel is-running">
			<h3>{{#if isHosted}}Copying your campaign data{{else}}Migrating{{/if}}</h3>
			<p>{{progress.label}}{{#if progress.total}} ({{progress.index}} of {{progress.total}}){{/if}}</p>
			<p class="stonetop-migration-note">
				{{#if isHosted}}Leave this tab alone until it finishes.
				{{else}}Leave this tab alone until Foundry returns you to the setup screen.{{/if}}
			</p>
		</section>
	{{/if}}

	{{#if isPrepared}}
		<section class="stonetop-migration-panel">
			<h3>Data copied. One step left.</h3>
			<p class="stonetop-migration-counts">
				{{prepared.documents}} documents and {{prepared.settings}} settings copied,
				across {{prepared.locations}} places in this world.
			</p>
			<p>Now point the world itself at the renamed system, using your host's own tools:</p>
			<ol>
				<li>Export this world and save the zip.</li>
				<li>Unzip it and open <code>world.json</code> inside.</li>
				<li>
					Change <code>"system": "{{this.oldId}}"</code> to <code>"system": "{{this.newId}}"</code>,
					and save the file.
				</li>
				<li>Re-import that folder through your host's import wizard.</li>
				<li>Launch it as GM. It finishes on its own; refresh the page once if it asks.</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="stonetop-migration-note">
				Until you do all that, this world keeps running on <code>{{this.oldId}}</code> exactly as
				it did before, and re-opening this window will simply tell you there is nothing
				left to copy.
			</p>
		</section>
	{{/if}}

	{{#if isFailed}}
		<section class="stonetop-migration-panel is-blocked">
			<h3>That did not finish</h3>
			<p>{{this.error}}</p>
		</section>
	{{/if}}

	<footer class="stonetop-migration-actions">
		{{#if isPrepared}}
			<button type="button" data-action="dismiss">Close</button>
		{{else if isConfirming}}
			<button type="button" data-action="confirm">Yes, migrate now</button>
			<button type="button" data-action="cancel">Cancel</button>
		{{else if isReady}}
			{{#if isHosted}}
				<button type="button" data-action="prepare">Prepare this world</button>
			{{else}}
				<button type="button" data-action="migrate">Migrate this world</button>
			{{/if}}
			<button type="button" data-action="dismiss">Not now</button>
		{{/if}}
		{{#if canRecheck}}
			<button type="button" data-action="recheck">Check again</button>
		{{/if}}
	</footer>
</div>
